      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-11-21_WidnesExaminer_art0042" n="art0042">
        <head>Liver Disorder, Chest Pain, and Indigestion</head>
        <p>Liver Disorder, Chest Pain, and Indigestion</p>
        <p>Cured.</p>
        <p>Have you ever been the " talk of the village," or town ? Frequently the distinction belongs to crack footballers, but William Maakrey, of Hawthorn Cottage, Lietley (Crewe), was, a short time back, in this most enviable position. A " Crewe Chronicle " reporter, writing recently on the subject, states :—"Io the course of an interview I had with him, Mr Maskrey said :—' I am a miner and some time back began to be ailing. My liver became out of order, and I exnerienced great difficulty in breathing. After meals I was subject to great pain across my chest, due no doubt to indigestion. I also suffered agony from pains under my sh Io the morning, when I got up, I felt St for nothing. I was even more tired than when I went to bed the previ- ous night. This state of affairs continued so long that °Weenie very low-spirited and melancholy ; and fort sevral days at a time I would be quite unable to go in nay work. Nearly every day I had a frigntfta</p>
        <p>biliotig .a, could not take Bey food. I was attended by several doctors, but did not derive mesh b?..nelit from their treatment. I had given up all Isobel of ever getting butter, when times-arrived at my house a book telling of what Chas. Forde's Bile Beans bad done in cases similar to mine. I thought I would give them a trial and I was soon glad I had done so, for as I went on with them the pains in my chest and under my shoulders gradually began:to disappear, and nip sleep ceased to be disturbed. In the mornings I awakened greatly refreshed aid able to leave for my work as cueerful as anybody could wish. They have now corn- cutely cured me of all my ailments and my case and my pere nave been the talk of the village." _</p>
        <p>This is the kind of event whin has made for Bile Beans a world-aide reputation. If y(sit're suffering from any of the following diseases, try rheas ! They have been found to be a curs for indigestion, liver and kidney disorder, constipation, piles, headache, debility, dizziness, pains in the chest, nerareusness, female eilments, colds, chill, rheumatism, and a preventive of influenza. All chemists stock them, or you may ob- tain them direct from the Bile Bean Manufacturing Co., Red Cross-street, London, E.C., by sending prices, Is or 24 9i per box (2a 91 box contains 3 times Is lid).</p>
