        <p>ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL. SANKEY AMATEURS v STRETTON A.F.O. This match was played on Stretton ground in fair weather. The Amateurs won the toss and Po well kicked off with a strong wind. After five minutes play the Amateurs scored the first goal. Some exciting play followed, but nothing resulted. Half-time :—Amateurs, 1 ; Stretton, 0. At the restart the homesters made some dangerous rushes, but were checked by the visitors' full back. About three minutes from time Stretton scored, putting both sides equal. Both team tried hard to obtain the lead, the visitors having very hard lines. Final : Amateurs, 1 ;.Stretton, 1. WILDERSPOOL CENTRAL V. ST MART'S RESERVE. Played at Arpley on Saturday. In the first half Wilderspool thoroug blv overplayed the Saints,andiat half-Lime the score stood : Wilderspool Central, five goals; St Mary's Reserve, nil. The second half was more keenly fought, and each side scoring a goal, Wilderspool ran out winners by six goals to one. WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT LEAG UR. FIRST DIVIEION. WARRINGTON " GUARDIAN " V WARRINGTON ST PETER'S. These teams met at Arpley on Saturday. During the first half G Woodhead scored for the " Guardian " team, the score at half time being "Guardian" one goal ; St Peters, nil. On re-starting Phcenia equalised for St Peter's. Final :Guardian," one goal ; bt Peter's, one goal. •</p>
