        <p>Polling in the Orkney end Shetland by-election closed last evening. Ehe weather on Wedn*sday was fine, and the number (A those who voted is believed to be larger than at soy Jarevious contest. The ballot-boxes from the country districts will only reach Lerwick at She end of this week. They will be Fent to Kirkwall on Monday, and tne regult will he declared on Tuesday. The mail trains arriving at Calais from Paris on Wed- mere covered with snow, and the cold was so intense that the snow was frozen on the roofs aed foot- boards of the carriages.</p>
